    "prose": "Rain drummed harder beyond the workshop, and the wind pressed against the wide gate. Mert remained between Aya and the approach, keeping the safety boundary in place.\n\nAya faced him across the same restored mosaic panel. “Ready?”\n\n“On three,” Mert said. “Lift evenly, then hold.”\n\nAya resisted the urge to start early. She set herself at one side while Mert took the other.\n\n“One,” he counted. “Two. Three.”\n\nAya and Mert lifted the mosaic panel together. It rose level between them, intact, with both of them maintaining a steady two-person hold.\n\nThe weight pulled at Aya’s arms. She almost shifted ahead, but Mert said, “Stay there. Let me clear the approach first.”\n\nAya stopped herself and followed his coordination. “All right. I’m holding.”\n\nStill supporting his side of the panel, Mert changed his bodily position. He stepped away from his blocking place and opened the approach to the yard gate, explicitly releasing the safety boundary.\n\nAya saw him move clear. The way to the gate was no longer blocked, but she did not rush toward it.\n\n“Boundary released,” Mert said. “We move only when we’re both set.”\n\nAya checked that their shared hold remained level. Rain swept across the covered yard outside, louder now, but the panel stayed safely inside the workshop.\n\n“We’re both set,” she said, keeping her side steady. “And we go together.”\n\nThey remained in the workshop with the same fragile panel raised between them, ready for the next coordinated move.",
